\title{CCS and the Unified View}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Customisable constraint systems, proposed as the generalisation that has R1CS, Plonkish, and AIR as instances. Worth understanding both as a claim about expressiveness and as the format HyperNova folds.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The definition, and the explicit embeddings of the three formats into it.}
        \li{What the unification buys: one folding scheme, one commitment interface, one soundness proof.}
        \li{What it costs — where a CCS encoding is asymptotically or concretely worse than the native format.}
        \li{Whether the same unification is the right structuring principle for a formal library, or whether [ArkLib](dhsorens-0040)'s per-system files are better.}
    }
}
